  "lineage": "Sikh hymn form set to the raga headings of the Guru Granth Sahib, formalised by Guru Nanak and Guru Arjan in 16th–17th century Punjab and revived as Gurmat Sangeet by 20th-century scholars such as Bhai Avtar Singh and Gurnam Singh — sung by a ragi jatha of two harmoniums and a tabla (historically rabab, taus and dilruba with jori), in medium-slow teental or ektaal, with the sthai/rahao line as a returning refrain and plain syllabic delivery favouring textual clarity over Hindustani ornament.",
